        "children": [],
        "responseSpace": "given",
        "answerSpaceMm": null
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q1",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "In the following, we consider cross-sections of the bundles of canisters. When canisters are bundled, two types of region are important. These are shown below by the shading. The radius of each circle is 2.5 cm.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [
          {
            "id": "p27-q1-regions",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"regionBlue\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the requested interstitial regions\"}],\"reference\":\"page 27 Packaging Diagrams 1 and 2\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,line width=0.8pt]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{regionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\fill[regionBlue] (-2.5,0) arc (180:90:2.5) arc (270:180:2.5)--cycle;\n\\draw (0,0) circle (2.5) (0,5) circle (2.5);\\draw (-2.5,0) rectangle (2.5,5);\\node[below] at (0,-3){Diagram 1};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 29.529057768682467,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 27,
              "sourceRegion": "Diagram 1",
              "description": "Two vertically tangent circles and the square side; only the left interstice is shaded.",
              "mathematics": "All circles have radius 2.5 cm. Diagram 1 uses a half-square minus two quadrants; Diagram 2 uses an equilateral triangle minus three 60-degree sectors.",
              "answerVisibility": "No calculated lengths or areas supplied."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-q1-regions-diagram2",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"regionBlue\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the requested interstitial regions\"}],\"reference\":\"page 27 Packaging Diagrams 1 and 2\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,line width=0.8pt]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{regionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\n\\fill[regionBlue] (2.5,0) arc (180:120:2.5) arc (300:240:2.5) arc (60:0:2.5)--cycle;\n\\draw (0,0) circle (2.5) (5,0) circle (2.5) (2.5,{2.5*sqrt(3)}) circle (2.5);\n\\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(2.5,{2.5*sqrt(3)})--cycle;\\node[below] at (2.5,-3){Diagram 2};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 57.435460646838905,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 27,
              "sourceRegion": "Diagram 2",
              "description": "Three mutually tangent circles and the triangle joining their centres; the central curved gap is shaded.",
              "mathematics": "All circles have radius 2.5 cm. Diagram 1 uses a half-square minus two quadrants; Diagram 2 uses an equilateral triangle minus three 60-degree sectors.",
              "answerVisibility": "No calculated lengths or areas supplied."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p27-q1-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "Calculate the exact area of the shaded region in diagram 1.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{25}{2}-\\dfrac{25\\pi}{8}\\text{ cm}^2$",
              "worked": "The square has side $5$ cm. The shaded left half contains two quarter-circles removed from half the square.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12(5^2)-2\\left(\\frac14\\pi(2.5)^2\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{25}{2}-\\frac{25\\pi}{8}\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p27-q1-b",
            "type": "group",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q1-b-i",
                "type": "part",
                "label": "i",
                "prompt": "What is the side length of the triangle shown in diagram 2?",
                "layout": "list",
                "columns": null,
                "questionDiagrams": [],
                "children": [],
                "answer": {
                  "short": "$5\\text{ cm}$",
                  "worked": "Each side joins the centres of two touching circles: $2.5+2.5=5$ cm.",
                  "solutionDiagrams": []
                },
                "answerSpaceMm": 12
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q1-b-ii",
                "type": "part",
                "label": "ii",
                "prompt": "What is the height of the triangle? Calculate an exact answer.",
                "layout": "list",
                "columns": null,
                "questionDiagrams": [],
                "children": [],
                "answer": {
                  "short": "$\\dfrac{5\\sqrt3}{2}\\text{ cm}$",
                  "worked": "The altitude bisects the base of the equilateral triangle. By Pythagoras' theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+\\left(\\frac52\\right)^2&=5^2\\\\h^2&=25-\\frac{25}{4}\\\\h^2&=\\frac{75}{4}\\\\h&=\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{2}\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$",
                  "solutionDiagrams": []
                },
                "answerSpaceMm": 33
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q1-b-iii",
                "type": "part",
                "label": "iii",
                "prompt": "What is the exact area of the shaded region in diagram 2?",
                "layout": "list",
                "columns": null,
                "questionDiagrams": [],
                "children": [],
                "answer": {
                  "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac{25\\sqrt3}{4}-\\dfrac{25\\pi}{8}\\right)\\text{ cm}^2$",
                  "worked": "Subtract three $60^\\circ$ sectors from the equilateral triangle.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\frac12\\times5\\times\\frac{5\\sqrt3}{2}-3\\left(\\frac{60}{360}\\pi\\left(\\frac52\\right)^2\\right)\\\\A&=\\frac{25\\sqrt3}{4}-\\frac{25\\pi}{8}\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
                  "solutionDiagrams": []
                },
                "answerSpaceMm": 33
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
